    <item>
      <title>Open PDF Editor 0.1.1</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:10:04 +0000</pubDate>
      <link>https://github.com/purpleax/open-pdf-editor/releases/tag/v0.1.1</link>
      <sparkle:version>2</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
      <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://github.com/purpleax/open-pdf-editor/releases/tag/v0.1.1</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
      <description sparkle:format="markdown">Security fixes. PDFs with impossibly large pages can no longer crash the app or use up memory, and a deeply nested outline can no longer crash it. Saving an attachment now asks first when the file could contain an app or a script, and saved attachments are checked by macOS before they open. A document with a malformed date no longer crashes the inspector. Only real PDFs are opened, and a rare crash after showing or hiding a layer is fixed.</description>
